Double-square from rank 2/7: the target is always within the board (for a black pawn on a7: 8+32=40=a3, 40 & 0x88 = 40 & 136 = 0x28 & ... 40 = 0b101000, 136 = 0b10001000 → AND = 0b101000 & 0b10001000 = 0. OK). So the double-square `to` is always on-board if single `to` is on-board. But for safety, the double-square branch is nested inside the `if (!this._board[to])` of the single move — and the single move is now guarded. If the single `to` is off-board (rank 8/1 pawns), the double-square is skipped anyway, and SECOND_RANK won't match for rank 8/1. So guarding only the single move is sufficient.

Hmm wait, one more consideration: are there other paths that could generate off-board pawn moves? En passant: `to === this._epSquare` — epSquare is a valid square. OK.

Also, for a white pawn on h8, the captures loop has `if (to & 0x88) continue` — to = -10 → -10 & 0x88 = 0x00000080? -10 = 0xFFFFFFF6, & 0x88 = 0x80? 0xF6 = 1111_0110 & 1000_1000 = 1000_0000 = 0x80 ≠ 0 → skip. Good.

So the minimal fix: add `!(to & 0x88) &&` to the single-square branch.

